sometimes all it takes is one role to  change your career this is especially  true of sean william scott who became a  huge star from american pie his role as  the crude rude dim-witted dude stiffler  gained him enough notoriety that would  impact his career forever  before american pie sean william scott  himself was not a particularly  noteworthy performer he had zero feature  film credits to his name and his most  notable forays into performing were  appearing in a sunny delight commercial  and an aerosmith video at age 28 he was  working at the home depot and going on  lots of auditions and it was that  conviction that eventually resulted in  american pie part of his early struggles  can be attributed to how scott initially  saw himself scott told nbc in 2008 i  always anticipated having a career in  sports but movies were my passion i was  reminded that i could have a life  outside of being a stressed out  professional athlete i realized i could  use the same work ethic and apply it to  another career that i love i graduated  early told my coaches i wasn't going to  play sports anymore and moved to la i  got lucky got a manager and that was  that  when scott was first hired for the role  of stiffler it hadn't been written as a  major character in fact stiffler only  had a passing presence in the story  scott told entertainment weekly in 2019  the stiffler character was in two or  three scenes and he was written to be  such an  hole that i was like i don't even know  if i'd want to play this guy so i was  like i'm going to rewrite a bit of it  make him the guy you hate to love he's  probably insecure he's like the guy who  wants to be loved the most  as it would turn out his meeker scripted  presence in the production resulted in a  mediocre payday despite portraying a fan  favorite character in the sex comedy  scott only scored eight thousand dollars  for playing the role  the summer of 1999 began with moviegoers  counting down the days to the first new  star wars movie in 16 years by the end  of that season many had shifted to  discussions of the over-the-top ranch of  american pie a good deal of this talk  involved sean william scott who embodied  a classic version of abrasive masculine  immaturity and whose commitment to the  part turned what could have been a  nuisance into a fan favorite scott's  appeal as stiffler was so strong that it  even lasted well into the various pie  sequels while reviewing 2012's american  reunion roger ebert mentioned his  affinity for scots stiffler while  calling him a highlight of the film  ebert shared sean william scott has made  the role of stiffler his own and seems  able to morph his face into an entirely  new person narrowed eyes broad maniacal  grin frightening focus still with all  the zeal for seduction and adventure he  had in high school the ingenuity with  which he destroys the jet skis of two  jerks can only be admired even in these  more enlightened times a 2019  retrospective review of the original  american pie that criticized the  feature's politically incorrect elements  still found time to praise scott's  performance years removed from when  american pie first hit theaters scott  can still drum up enough praise to  remind everyone why he became the film's  biggest breakout star  in the wake of american pie scott's  status as an actor was significantly  elevated his first appearance in 2000's  original final destination was a brief  one that had him meeting a graphic  demise on screen after that scott  headlined the todd phillips feature road  trip another raunchy comedy that cast  him among a group of students who hit  the road in pursuit of sexual delights  other roles around this time included  dude where's my car and evolution all  playing off the dim horny jock persona  he suddenly had all to himself it's an  age-old hollywood question do you lean  into your notoriety and risk the  diminishing returns of repetition or do  you try to blaze a unique path and risk  alienating your newfound fans scott  shared in 2003 about his struggle with  such questions saying i was like nah  being the funny guy that's not why i  came to la but i appreciated it and i  realized that this is really just a  blessing to be able to make people laugh  when a comedy becomes as successful as  american pie it's only a matter of time  before talk turns to a sequel pi  presented a pair almost immediately the  first of these arrived in 2001 under the  name american pie 2. a smash hit its  success got american wedding greenlit  which would arrive in 2003. suddenly the  franchise wasn't about teenage sexual  escapades anymore but instead watching  the characters navigate various stages  of young adulthood through it all  stifler remained an anchor of immaturity  who could always be counted on for crazy  antics and ill-advised situations  scott admitted in 2003 i don't know why  people like the character it's because  of the way his friends played off that  character because if they would have  dismissed him and just treated him as  another doll as an audience member you'd  be like whoa he's just a jerk but they  just play with him and they accept what  he does  you're very unpleasant individually know  that  while films like 2001's jay and silent  bob strike back in 2003's old school  cast scott and supporting roles he also  got plenty of opportunities to become a  leading man in 2003 he was cast opposite  fellow rising star dwayne the rock  johnson in peterborough's so-so the  rundown he also signed on for 2005's  high profile reboot of the dukes of  hazzard despite a massive ad campaign  dukes bombed both critically and at the  box office a string of ill-conceived  comedies followed many trying to  recapture that stifler magic 2007's  american loser cast him opposite  gretchen mull as a rudderless adolescent  adult that same year mr woodcock put him  opposite billy bob thornton as an adult  looking to get revenge for his  adolescence 2008's the promotion had  scott competing with john c reilly to  get past the adolescent ways that had  stopped them from advancing in their  careers  in 2008 however scott made a dent with  paul rudd on one of his first star  vehicles role models trying to put some  space between his model's character and  stiffler scott said at the time  he's not really mean to anybody he's  actually a very optimistic guy but  clearly the whole physicality of it and  that vibe is very similar but i had  wanted to add something that made him a  little more irreverent role models  earned significantly better reviews than  hazard in scott's other films of this  period and also fared better at the box  office but still now a decade after his  american pie breakthrough sean william  scott was still trying to overcome the  same typecasting limitations  like many other comedic actors before  him sean william scott tried to branch  out with more serious films it was a  smart endeavor but unfortunately it  seems he may have just bet on the wrong  horses his big high profile leading man  play was undoubtedly bulletproof monk  the 2003 film was based on a comic book  it was also the directorial debut of  in-demand  [Music]  to answer that question ask yourself  when was the last time you heard anyone  talk about bulletproof monk around the  same time he signed up for what was a  very in-demand movie southland tales it  was filmmaker richard kelly's feverishly  anticipated follow-up to donnie darko a  movie that seemed to have announced the  arrival of hollywood's newest auteur  unfortunately the production became  notoriously troubled the film was  rumored to be largely incoherent and  after years of delays was released with  little fanfare in more recent years  scott has appeared in the grisly  thriller bloodline and a crime drama  already gone but neither of them fared  much better  in 2010 sean william scott kicked off a  new decade by connecting with one of the  most prolific names in 1990s indie  cinema filmmaker kevin smith probably  seemed like a safe bet as did starring  opposite the legendary bruce willis what  scott most likely didn't anticipate  however was a troubled production that  had the original title dropped against  smith's wishes the director and leading  man coming to despise each other and the  entire experience being so miserable  that smith hasn't made a studio film  since  scott was however one of the funnier  parts of the finished film despite  cop-out faring poorly with critics and  the box office it did earn the actor a  dream role well maybe smith even  considered his collaboration with scott  to be the inspiration he needed to push  hit somebody a hockey comedy based on a  warren zevonne song across the goal line  in 2010 smith explained sean for me was  the key into the character this dude has  something in him that you can just see  hang so well on buddy he's got some pain  that's going to work out well as you may  have guessed hit somebody has still not  made the leap from the page to the  silver screen it was going to be two  movies then one movie again then a mini  series and eventually smith just read  the script on his podcast in 2018.  whether the film is ever resurrected and  whether scott will still play the part  seems doubtful at this point fortunately  if you want to see scott in the world of  hockey we still have his two goon films  in 2013 sean william scott returned to  the role that had made him a household  name with american reunion it was the  fourth installment of the franchise and  had the american pie gang returned for  more raunchy escapades this gave scott  the opportunity to return to the role of  stiffler now a decade older but only  marginally wiser  yeah that's perfect scott didn't need  any compulsion to come back to the  franchise that made him in fact  according to him it was his idea he  shared it was a long time in the making  because i pitched the movie three years  ago the idea of bringing everybody back  for a high school reunion i said three  years to go wow how much fun is it going  to be to play stiffler in his 30s it was  a blast two decades after his american  pie breakthrough scott is still a  working actor although it's hard to  argue that any of his several dozen  roles has come close to stiffler as far  as mass appeal and awareness in 2018 he  took over the lead role in the fox cop  show lethal weapon though he was coming  on to a program brought with behind the  scenes drama scott's presence on the  show gave it a much needed positive  boost in publicity intriguingly scott  apparently pursued the role himself once  he saw that the show's original lead  claim crawford had been fired by the  program though lethal weapon with scott  in the lead role lasted just one season  that wasn't the end of his tv work later  in 2021 he'll be back on the fox network  with welcome to flatch a docu-comedy  that aims to be the office for small  town america a comedic project flash  seems like it could represent a  fundamental shift in scott's career as  he plays an authority figure and the  lives of some younger troublemakers  perhaps this is the beginning of sean  william scott reinventing himself as a  middle-aged actor whose days of  frivolity are behind him  it has now been well over two decades  since scott's life was changed forever  through the antics of stifler in  american pie though it has had its ups  and downs he has insisted that he has no  regrets about the career launching role  scott said in 2018 i didn't think martin  scorsese was going to cast me in his  next movie i understood why i wasn't  getting cast for other things i would  have been a distraction i kind of  pigeonholed myself but i felt really  lucky to get the chance to make people  laugh given that the combined worldwide  grosses of his movies have exceeded 1  billion dollars it is hard to feel too  bad for sean william scott some gambles  have paid off others have not but talk  to any actor and they'll most likely  tell you they'd be happy to have a  decades-long career with more than 30 tv  and film projects under their belt as  scott himself put it in 2018 i just got  lucky with american pie that movie gave  me a career  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite celebrities are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

